    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Tyler Soderstrom** headlining our offensive attack. Sporting an elite 75.57 score, **Soderstrom** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Walbert Ure\u00f1a, where an 18% boost in SP skill projection and favorable platoon splits make him our strongest play. We also expect significant production from **Corbin Carroll** (68.93) and **Josh Naylor** (66.55); **Carroll** thrives in his #2 hole despite a tough matchup against Robbie Ray, while **Naylor** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill lift against Noah Schultz. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (65.94) and **James Wood** (65.34) round out our core, with **Pasquantino** capitalizing on a projected wind-out scenario and a positive platoon edge against Sonny Gray.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was benching **Mickey Moniak**. While his 55.76 score was compelling, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a restrictive 15% penalty on his platoon split against MacKenzie Gore, which outweighed the park factor bonuses. We remain cautious with **Zach McKinstry** (49.35), who carries a lingering 41% rain risk; he earns a start primarily due to his utility in stolen base opportunities against the slow delivery of Slade Cecconi, but he remains a high-variance play. With lineups still pending across the board, the reliance on projected batting positions\u2014specifically the premium placed on **James Wood** batting leadoff\u2014is the primary variable. We are keeping a close eye on **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**, whose sub-55 scores reflect the volatility of the back-end lineup spots; should these confirmations shift, we are prepared to pivot to our bench depth to ensure we maximize our daily game caps.",
